Pi-hole is a network-wide ad blocker: a DNS server for the whole local
network that answers queries for advertising and tracking domains with a
blackhole address, so every device behind it is protected without any
software of its own. It comes with a web interface for its statistics,
query log, lists and settings, and the pihole command-line tool.

This is the native FreeBSD port, from the FreedomNAS forks that carry the
FreeBSD support. The DNS engine is in dns/pihole-ftl.
